  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13960647",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-70425",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form",
      "problem": "Let $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,-3).$ Find $|a+2b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=i+3j-3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a+2b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(2i+j)+2(i+3j-3k) \\\\  & =4i+7j-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+2b| & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+49+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{101}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
